candidate.question:
A clinic needs the appropriate rapid differential-diagnosis examination for a 63-year-old with three weeks of painless jaundice, dark urine and pale stools, plus an electromagnetic-interference- and noise-immune image link. Packages (upfront/annual costs, $thousands):
1: abdominal sonography/fiber optic, 100/40;
2: abdominal sonography/fiber optic, 150/10;
3: abdominal sonography/copper, 50/5;
4: abdominal CT/fiber optic, 60/5.
Within-modality capabilities are otherwise equivalent. Each has three year-end annual payments; discount annually at 10%; no other costs or residual values.
Which eligible package minimizes present-value cost, and what is that cost (nearest $0.01 thousand)?

